					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="catbg"><font class="catbg" size="2">Started by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Gnos">Gnos</a> | Last post by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Kinladar">Kinladar</a></font></td>
					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#F8F8F8" valign="top" height="40" class="windowbg2">I said it in guild chat last night, and I'll repeat it here, I really have no opinion about the name, it's not that important to me.<br /><br />What's important about any guild is it's accomplishments, the name isn't that big a deal to me. <br /><br />Let's look at it this way, it's the group of people in Anth/Wow/AoM/FoT that have gotten to Elemental Raiding status regardless of the guild tags involved. What other guilds have done this?<br /><br />1) Ascent (More like PoT guild)<br />2) EIE/DA<br />3) Arirang<br />4) FoT (As it will now be known)<br /><br />Not sure what other servers have 4 elemantal guilds, but even with all the Drama on Rodcet, there are some damned talented people who play on this server, (note, I didn't say guild, I said server) regardless of all the BS.<br /><br />Each guild has things to be proud of, and each guild does things it's own way. I just don't care to get into pissing matches over it all.</td>
					</tr><tr>
