						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="catbg"><font class="catbg" size="2">Started by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Gnos">Gnos</a> | Last post by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Gnos">Gnos</a></font></td>
					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#F8F8F8" valign="top" height="40" class="windowbg2">How long have you known me Pepa?&nbsp; Would I <i>ever</i> try to fight an unarmed opponent? <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/rolleyes.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Reason I show interest is this:&nbsp; I have friends who were in Anthology for a long time.&nbsp; Anthology (and the guilds that predated it) was one of the guilds I looked up to as I was coming up.&nbsp; I respected them for their ability to figure out good tactics and their unwillingness to just throw large numbers of people at a mob.<br />Then Anthology started slowing down and instead of recruiting more they merge with another guild.&nbsp; Now this in itself isn't a problem, but the 180 degree turn in the way they conduct themselves is the problem.<br />Even if one over looked the zerg portion of it, you now have:<br /><ul><li>Bigger idiots in high level zones<br /><li>Really stupid guild names<br /><li>The lose of some really good players from the guild<br /><li>Newer people to the guild flaming the ones that leave</ul><br /><br />Now if after all this you don't understand, well you can<br /><marquee>Go to hell you zerg loving bastard</marquee></td>
					</tr><tr>
